{
 "title": "Solving x² − 5x + 6 = 0",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "The equation",
   "say": "We need to solve the quadratic equation x squared minus five x plus six equals zero.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "eq",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 120,
     "text": "x² − 5x + 6 = 0",
     "size": 56,
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Try factoring",
   "say": "First, let's try factoring. We look for two numbers that multiply to 6 and add to −5.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "fac1",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 260,
     "text": "Factor: find m, n such that",
     "size": 36
    },
    {
     "id": "fac2",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 320,
     "text": "m · n = 6   and   m + n = −5",
     "size": 36
    },
    {
     "id": "fac3",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 400,
     "text": "Try: −2 and −3?",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Check the factors",
   "say": "(−2)(−3) = 6 and (−2) + (−3) = −5. It works! So we can factor as (x − 2)(x − 3) = 0.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "chk",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 480,
     "text": "(−2)(−3) = 6  ✓\n(−2) + (−3) = −5  ✓",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "green"
    },
    {
     "id": "facform",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 580,
     "text": "(x − 2)(x − 3) = 0",
     "size": 44,
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Switch to quadratic formula",
   "say": "But let's switch to a simpler, more general method midway: the quadratic formula. It always works.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "switch",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 680,
     "text": "Switch to quadratic formula:",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "id": "formula",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 740,
     "text": "x = [ −b ± √(b² − 4ac) ] / (2a)",
     "size": 40
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Identify coefficients",
   "say": "Here a = 1, b = −5, and c = 6. Substitute these into the formula.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "coef",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 820,
     "text": "a = 1,  b = −5,  c = 6",
     "size": 40
    },
    {
     "id": "sub",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 880,
     "text": "x = [ 5 ± √(25 − 24) ] / 2",
     "size": 40,
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Simplify",
   "say": "The discriminant is 25 − 24 = 1, so the square root is 1. Thus x = (5 ± 1) / 2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "disc",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 940,
     "text": "Discriminant: 25 − 24 = 1",
     "size": 36
    },
    {
     "id": "simp",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 1000,
     "text": "x = (5 ± 1) / 2",
     "size": 44,
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Two solutions",
   "say": "This gives two solutions: x = (5 + 1)/2 = 3 and x = (5 − 1)/2 = 2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "sol1",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 1080,
     "text": "x = (5 + 1)/2 = 3",
     "size": 40
    },
    {
     "id": "sol2",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 1140,
     "text": "x = (5 − 1)/2 = 2",
     "size": 40
    },
    {
     "id": "final",
     "x": 400,
     "y": 1220,
     "text": "Solutions: x = 2 or x = 3",
     "size": 48,
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}